The eventual FPMD simulations were conducted in the canonical ensemble using a modified Langevin equation with a discretized integration timestep of 1.0~fs. Specifically, a cubic cell consisting of 1000 silicon atoms subject to periodic boundary conditions was considered. Using these settings we have performed in total 10 FPMD simulations, each 1.25~ns long, whose temperatures were ranging from its semiconducting crystalline state at 300~K up to its metallic liquid phase at 3000~K. 

The 3D Voronoi tesselation is performed using the Voro++ library \cite{rycroft2009voro++, lu2023extension}, which permits the computation of Voronoi cells and all their corresponding normal vectors for each particle individually. 

