\subsection{Dermatology IQA dataset}

\subsubsection{Data collection}

For the evaluation of our IQA models on dermatology image quality assessment (DIQA), we created a new dataset, named Legit.Health-DIQA-Artificial. This dataset was generated by selecting 100 pristine dermatology images and applying a set of artificial distortions (Figure \ref{fig:legithealth-diqa-distortions}). Each distortion was applied with different levels of strength, resulting in 1800 additional images in total. The distortions were inspired by that used for Kadid-10k \cite{lin2019kadid}: JPEG compression (3 levels), Gaussian blur (1), pixelation (2), sharpening (3), brightness (4), color (2), and contrast (3).

