\subsection{Asymmetric Type Space}
\label{Sec_AsyType}

In a recent paper, \citet{bikhchandani2022selling} study a two-product monopoly pricing problem under the following two sets of constraints on $\mathcal{X}$ and $\mathcal{Q}$, both parameterized by $\gamma\in [0,1]$:
\begin{itemize}
\item Decreasing marginal values (DMV): $\mathcal{X}=\{\mathbf{x}\in [0,1]^{2}:x_{2}\leq \gamma x_{1}\}$, $\mathcal{Q}=[0,1]^{2}$.
\item Increasing marginal values (IMV): $\mathcal{X}=\{\mathbf{x}\in [0,1]^{2}:x_{1}\leq \gamma x_{2}\}$, $\mathcal{Q}=\{\mathbf{q}\in [0,1]^{2}:q_{1}\geq q_{2}\}$.
\end{itemize}

\Cref{Thm_Active} can be invoked to produce two of their main propositions.

\begin{corollary}[\citet{bikhchandani2022selling}]
\label{Cor_BM}
Under DMV, $\mathbf{q}$ is active only if $q_{1}=1$ (Proposition 1). Under IMV, $\mathbf{q}$ is active only if $q_{1}=q_{2}$ (Proposition 7).
\end{corollary}

