% 先前比较大脑活动模式与人工智能表征的研究通常依赖于具有固定参数的单一相似性指标，而没有系统地研究测量尺度如何影响人工系统与生物系统之间观察到的对应关系。虽然我们的分析表明，不同的相似性指标之间存在显著的一致性（图~\ref{fig:metric_consistency}），但测量尺度的选择可能揭示两个系统中重要的组织原则，而这些原则原本可能被隐藏。
Previous research comparing brain activity patterns with AI representations has typically relied on single alignment metrics with fixed parameters, without systematically investigating how measurement scale impacts the observed correspondence between artificial and biological systems. While our analyses demonstrated significant consistency across different measures (Figure~\ref{fig:metric_consistency}), the choice of measurement scale may nonetheless reveal important organizational principles in both systems that would otherwise remain hidden. 

% 为了探索这种可能性，我们系统地将CKA测量中的核大小从较小尺度调整到较大尺度，结果发现了一个显著的变化，即大脑区域表现出最强的模型对应关系（图~\ref{fig:kernel_analysis}a）。这种方法论具有直接的生物学意义：较小的核尺寸（较低的σ值）关注的是不同刺激之间非常相似的激活模式，捕捉到高度特异性的表征相似性，类似于初级感觉区域对特定特征的选择性反应。相比之下，较大的核尺寸（较高的σ值）能够检测更多样刺激之间的相似性，反映出更广泛的表征模式，类似于联想皮层在不同情境下整合不同信息的方式。
To explore this possibility, we systematically varied the kernel size in our CKA measurements from smaller to larger scales, uncovering a striking shift in which brain regions showed strongest model correspondence (Figure~\ref{fig:kernel_analysis}a). This methodological approach has direct biological significance: smaller kernel sizes (lower $\sigma$ values) focus on very similar activation patterns across stimuli, capturing highly specific representational similarities analogous to how primary sensory areas respond selectively to specific features. In contrast, larger kernel sizes (higher $\sigma$ values) detect similarities across more varied stimuli, reflecting broader representational patterns similar to how association cortices integrate diverse information across contexts.

% 使用根据 Yeo-7 网络分类法 ~\cite{yeo2011organization} 分组的 HCP\_MMP1~\cite{glasser2016multi} 分区，我们观察到随着内核大小的增加，主要视觉区域的相对对齐明显下降，而边缘、腹侧注意和默认模式网络的对齐则增加。
Using the HCP\_MMP1~\cite{glasser2016multi} parcellation grouped according to the Yeo-7 network taxonomy~\cite{yeo2011organization}, we observed that as kernel size increased, primary visual areas showed substantial decreases in relative alignment, while limbic, ventral attention, and default mode networks showed increasing alignment. 

% 随着核尺寸的增加，对齐度下降最为显著的是早期视觉区域 V1 ($\Delta = -5.30$), V2 ($\Delta = -2.81$) 和 V3 ($\Delta = -1.05$)，而最强的增加发生在边缘区域，包括眶额皮质 (OFC, $\Delta = +1.56$), 颞区 TF ($\Delta = +1.36$), TE2a ($\Delta = +1.36$) 和 TGv ($\Delta = +1.33$)，以及海马旁回区域 EC ($\Delta = +1.09$) 和 PeEc ($\Delta = +1.06$)。
The most dramatic decreases in alignment with increasing kernel size were observed in early visual areas V1 ($\Delta = -5.30$), V2 ($\Delta = -2.81$), and V3 ($\Delta = -1.05$), while the strongest increases occurred in limbic regions including orbital frontal cortex (OFC, $\Delta = +1.56$), temporal regions TF ($\Delta = +1.36$), TE2a ($\Delta = +1.36$), and TGv ($\Delta = +1.33$), and parahippocampal regions EC ($\Delta = +1.09$) and PeEc ($\Delta = +1.06$).

% 这些变化在受试者之间非常一致，所有大脑区域的标准化对齐变化的符号一致性为 0.83，这表明了信息在大脑中以不同尺度呈现的基本原理。
These shifts were remarkably consistent across subjects, with a sign consistency of 0.83 in normalized alignment changes across all brain regions, suggesting a fundamental principle in how information is represented at different scales in the brain. 

% 图~\ref{fig:kernel_analysis}b 在皮质表面可视化了这种转变，揭示了在不同核大小下，对齐模式从后到前（枕叶到额叶）的梯度变化。皮质可视化展示了语言和视觉模型在多种核大小下归一化的大脑对齐分数。对于语言模型，与主要视觉区域相比，颞叶和前额叶区域的对齐更强，尤其是在核大小较大的情况下。视觉模型显示出类似的模式，但后视觉区域的对齐相对较强。差异图 ($\Delta$) 突出显示了语言和视觉模型在大脑对齐方面存在差异的区域，红色表示语言模型对齐更强，蓝色表示视觉模型对齐更强。
This shift was visualized on the cortical surface in Figure~\ref{fig:kernel_analysis}b, revealing a gradient from posterior-to-anterior (occipital to frontal lobe) in alignment patterns at different kernel sizes. The cortical visualizations display the normalized brain alignment scores for both language and vision models across multiple kernel sizes. For language models, stronger alignment is visible in temporal and prefrontal regions compared to primary visual areas, particularly at larger kernel sizes. Vision models show similar patterns but with relatively stronger alignment in posterior visual areas. The difference maps ($\Delta$) highlight regions where language and vision models differ in their brain alignment, with red indicating stronger language model alignment and blue indicating stronger vision model alignment.

% 随着核大小的增加，这种从后到前的梯度在所有受试者中变得更加明显，前部区域在较大尺度下表现出相对较强的对齐。这种差异在额叶和颞叶区域的语言模型中尤为明显，且核大小最大。补充材料中提供了所有四个受试者的可视化结果以及其他核大小设置。
As kernel size increases, this posterior-to-anterior gradient becomes more pronounced across all subjects, with anterior regions showing relatively stronger alignment at larger scales. This differentiation is particularly evident for language models in frontal and temporal lobes at the largest kernel sizes. Visualizations for all four subjects and additional kernel size settings are provided in the supplementary materials.


% 这些发现揭示了生物系统和人工系统共同遵循的基本组织原则：当信息流经处理通路时，表征会从局部的、特征特定的编码（由初级感觉区域的小尺度分析捕捉）转变为分布式的、依赖于上下文的结构，而后者在更高关联区域的大尺度分析中更容易捕捉。在语言模型中观察到的更强的尺度依赖性调制进一步表明，语言处理的表征尺度本质上比视觉更广泛，这反映了在大脑中观察到的层级信息处理模式。
These findings reveal a fundamental organizational principle shared by biological and artificial systems: as information flows through processing pathways, representations transition from local, feature-specific encodings—captured by smaller-scale analyses in primary sensory regions—to distributed, context-dependent structures better captured at larger scales in higher association areas. The stronger scale-dependent modulation observed in language models further suggests that language processing operates at inherently broader representational scales than vision, mirroring hierarchical information processing patterns observed in the brain.



