\section*{Methods}


% Topical subheadings are allowed. Authors must ensure that their Methods section includes adequate experimental and characterization data necessary for others in the field to reproduce their work.

To systematically investigate brain-AI alignment, we developed a comprehensive analytical framework combining neuroimaging and machine learning techniques. This approach quantifies similarities between neural activity patterns in human brains and internal representations in AI models using Centered Kernel Alignment (CKA)~\cite{kornblith2019similarity}, a robust similarity metric that accounts for different dimensionalities across systems. We analyzed fMRI responses from human subjects viewing natural images (Natural Scenes Dataset)~\cite{allen2022massive} alongside activations from 630 AI models (spanning vision and language domains) processing the same stimuli. By varying measurement parameters and examining alignment across different brain regions, model architectures, and training stages, we uncovered systematic patterns of representational convergence between biological and artificial systems. Statistical robustness was ensured through extensive validation across multiple subjects, metrics, and analytical parameters.

\subsection*{Data Acquisition and Preprocessing}
\paragraph{fMRI Data}
% 我们利用自然场景数据集 (NSD)~\cite{allen2022massive} 进行分析，这是一个大规模的 fMRI 数据集，用于捕捉对自然图像的神经反应。从数据集中的八名受试者中，我们选取​​了四名拥有完整数据轨迹的受试者（S01、S02、S05、S07）。每位受试者的数据包含对 24,980 个训练刺激（每位受试者独有）和 2,770 个测试刺激（所有受试者共享）的反应。为了在确保分析条件一致的前提下最大化数据量，我们主要分析的是训练集。
For our analysis, we utilized the Natural Scenes Dataset (NSD)~\cite{allen2022massive}, a large-scale fMRI dataset capturing neural responses to natural images. From the eight subjects in the dataset, we selected four (S01, S02, S05, S07) who had complete data trajectories. Each subject's data included responses to 24,980 training stimuli (unique per subject) and 2,770 testing stimuli (shared across subjects). To maximize data volume while ensuring consistent analysis conditions, we focused on the training set for our primary analyses.

% 我们遵循标准的 NSD 预处理流程，从预处理后的 \texttt{func1pt8mm} 数据中提取功能响应，该流程包括运动校正、畸变校正和血流动力学响应建模，以提取代表每个刺激神经响应的 beta 权重。所有分析均在受试者特定的功能空间中进行，以保留个体神经响应模式。
We extracted functional responses from the preprocessed \texttt{func1pt8mm} data following the standard NSD preprocessing pipeline, which includes motion correction, distortion correction, and hemodynamic response modeling to extract beta weights representing neural responses to each stimulus. All analyses were conducted in subject-specific functional space to preserve individual neural response patterns.

\paragraph{Stimulus Materials}
% NSD 刺激由来自 COCO 数据集 ~\cite{lin2014microsoft} 的图像组成，该数据集提供成对的图像-字幕注释。对于每幅图像，我们提取第一个可用的字幕作为语言模型的文本输入。这种方法能够使用相同的刺激在视觉和语言领域进行对齐的多模态分析，从而可以直接比较不同模态的神经表征。
The NSD stimuli consist of images from the COCO dataset~\cite{lin2014microsoft}, which provides paired image-caption annotations. For each image, we extracted the first available caption to serve as the textual input for language models. This approach enabled aligned multimodal analyses across vision and language domains using identical stimuli, allowing for direct comparison of neural representations across modalities.

\subsection*{Neural Network Models and Representation Extraction}

\paragraph{Language Models}
% 我们分析了 36 个涵盖不同架构和参数规模（5 亿至 720 亿个参数）的当代语言模型。我们的选择涵盖了主要的模型系列：Qwen~\cite{yang2024qwen2}、Llama~\cite{grattafiori2024llama}、Gemma~\cite{team2024gemma}、Mistral~\cite{yangMistral7B2023} 和 Phi~\cite{abdin2024phi} 等。为了探索不同微调方法的效果，我们纳入了 SimPO~\cite{meng2024simpo} 和 Tulu~\cite{lambert2024t} 等特殊变体。
We analyzed 36 contemporary language models spanning diverse architectures and parameter scales (500M to 72B parameters). Our selection included major model families: Qwen~\cite{yang2024qwen2}, Llama~\cite{grattafiori2024llama}, Gemma~\cite{team2024gemma}, Mistral~\cite{jiangMistral7B2023}, and Phi~\cite{abdin2024phi}, among others~\cite{team2023internlm}. To explore the effects of different fine-tuning approaches, we included specialized variants such as SimPO~\cite{meng2024simpo} and Tulu~\cite{lambert2024t}.

% 为了实现一致的表征提取，我们使用 HuggingFace Transformers 库 ~\cite{wolf-etal-2020-transformers} 和默认配置实现了所有模型。每个模型都使用其标准聊天模板处理图像字幕。例如，对于 Llama-3 模型，模板遵循以下结构：
For consistent representation extraction, we implemented all models using the HuggingFace Transformers library~\cite{wolf-etal-2020-transformers} with default configurations. Each model processed image captions using its standard chat template. For example, with Llama-3 models, the template followed this structure:

\begin{verbatim}
<|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>
