In physics, hysteresis refers to processes in which the state of a system depends on its past history---represented in this context by the input $y(t)$.
The extent of hysteresis is often characterized by the width or area of the hysteresis loop obtained when an appropriate system variable is plotted as a function of a switching parameter.\cite{hohl1995,jung1990}
