\begin{definition} Let $\delta=\delta_1\vert\ldots\vert\delta_k$ and $\tau=\tau_1\vert\ldots\vert\tau_\ell$ be two partitions of the set $\{1,\ldots,i\}$. Then 
\begin{itemize}
\item
$\delta$ and $\tau$ are  {\it compatible} if $k=\ell$ and for each $r$ there exists $s$ such that $\delta_r\subseteq \tau_s$ or $\tau_s\subseteq\delta_r$.

