\subsection{Case (ii): Temporal periodic modulation of the function of the linear potential}
Now, we consider a periodic time-dependent linear potential, given by $\Gamma(\tau) = \frac{1}{2P} \left[ 2 + 45\omega_1^2 \cos(\omega_1 \tau) \right]$, where $\omega_1$ is a real constant. Substituting this into the $X$-dependent relation in Eq. $(\ref{ex1})$, we obtain:
\begin{equation}
    X = \rho \sqrt{\frac{Q}{2P}} \left[ \zeta - 2d_3 P \tau - \tau^2 + 45 \cos(\omega_1 \tau) \right] + d_4,
\label{x2}
\end{equation}
where $d_3$ and $d_4$ are real constants. Using Eq. $(\ref{x2})$ along with the breather and positon solutions (Eqs. $(\ref{s1})$ and $(\ref{s2})$) for the KE equation, we can analyze the impact of a temporally periodic linear potential on the dynamics of breathers and positons.
