\subsubsection*{Open Models}
Publicly accessible models with permissive licensing (e.g., EleutherAI’s GPT-J, BigScience’s BLOOM) support broad developer collaboration, but may lack long-term support.

\subsubsection*{Proprietary Models}
Controlled models hosted by corporations like OpenAI and Meta, typically accessed via restricted APIs or exclusive partnerships, significantly shape market dynamics through platform lock-in.


