	\begin{abstract}
	Let $M$ be a closed connected oriented manifold admitting a non-zero degree map to a nilmanifold $f:M\longrightarrow N/\Gamma$. In the first part of the paper, we study effective finite group actions on $M$. In particular, we prove that $\Homeo(M)$ is Jordan, we bound the discrete degree of symmetry $\D(M)$ of $M$ (introduced in \cite{mundet2021topological}) and we study the number and the size of the stabilizers of an effective action of a finite group $G$ on $M$. We also study the toral rank conjecture and the Carlsson's conjecture for large primes for this class of manifolds. In the second part of the paper, we introduce the concepts of free iterated action of groups and iterated discrete degree of symmetry $\D_2(M)$, which refines $\D(M)$. We prove that if $N/\Gamma$ is a 2-step nilmanifold and $\D_2(M)=\D_2(N/\Gamma)$ then $H^*(M,\Q)\cong H^*(N/\Gamma,\Q)$.
	\end{abstract}
