One possible generalization of closed connected aspherical manifolds are closed connected admissible manifolds, which are manifolds where the only periodic self-homeomorphisms of $\tilde{M}$ commuting with the deck transformations group $\pi_1(M)$ are elements of $\Zc\pi_1(M)$. This class of manifolds include manifolds which admit a non-zero degree map to a closed aspherical manifold. Our first result is a straightforward generalization of \cref{main theorem1 intro}.

\begin{prop}\label{finite group actions admissible intro}
	Let $M$ be a closed connected admissible manifold. Assume that $\Out(\pi_1(M))$ is Minkowski and that $\Zc\pi_1(M)$ is finitely generated. Then:
	\begin{itemize}
		\item[1.] $\Homeo(M)$ is Jordan.
		\item[2.] $\D(M)\leq \rank\Zc\pi_1(M)/\operatorname{Torsion}(\Zc\pi_1(M))$.
		\item[3.] If $\chi(M)\neq 0$ and $\Aut(\pi_1(M))$ is Minkowski then $M$ is almost asymmetric.
		\item[4.] If $\Aut(\pi_1(M))$ is Minkowski then there exists a constant $C$ such that every finite group $G$ acting effectively on $M$ has a finite subgroup $H\leq G$ such that $[G:H]\leq C$ and $|\Stab(H,M)|\leq C$.
	\end{itemize}
\end{prop}

