Mountainous Disaster Scenario: An alert originates from a stationary node in a remote, mountainous region prone to avalanches (Verbier, the Jungfrau region, Andermatt, or Chur). These locations are characterised by lower train traffic and represent connectivity-challenged environments.\\

For all scenarios, the designated destination for the alert message was a fixed node located in Zurich, representing a national emergency response coordination centre.\\

